{"id": "8c40c6fa-03d7-4659-8393-3f1c1aa43868", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll pull cost data from Cost Explorer for both months, broken down by service and account, and figure out what's driving the increase.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_nxKP4ED9yd08NwH6LNCsUU", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Compare AWS costs between August 2026 and September 2026, and explain what drove the ~18% month-over-month increase the customer observed. Break the increase down by AWS service and by linked account.",
  "context": "Customer says their September bill was about 18% higher than August. They have Cost Explorer and CUR enabled. They want to know which services and which accounts (if multiple accounts/organization) contributed most to the increase, in dollar and percentage terms.",
  "resources": ["Use the Cost Explorer API (ce get_cost_and_usage) with UnblendedCost, Monthly granularity"],
  "timeframe": "August 2026 (2026-08-01 to 2026-09-01) vs September 2026 (2026-09-01 to 2026-10-01)",
  "criteria": "1) Get total cost for Aug and Sep to confirm overall % change. 2) Group by SERVICE (and by LINKED_ACCOUNT if more than one account exists in this org) for both months. 3) Compute the dollar and percent delta per service and per account between the two months. 4) Rank the top contributors to the increase (services/accounts with the largest absolute dollar increase). 5) Note any service that appeared in Sep but not Aug (new usage) or any large relative spike even if small in absolute dollars. 6) Return a concise structured summary: overall totals, top 5-8 services by delta, and per-account breakdown if multi-account, with dollar amounts and percentages."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Query AWS Cost Explorer for Aug vs Sep cost breakdown by service and account"}], "created_at": null}

